          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Musical Education</strong><br>\nMaurice Ravel was born on March 7, 1875, in Ciboure, France. He developed a fascination with music at an early age, taking piano lessons from his mother and composing his first pieces when he was just a child. He moved to Paris with his family and entered the Paris Conservatoire at the age of 14, where he studied piano and composition.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influences and Musical Style</strong><br>\nRavel's musical style was influenced by a variety of sources, including French baroque music, jazz, and Asian music. He was often associated with Impressionism, but he preferred to be seen as a classicist, drawing on a wide range of historical and cultural influences to create his unique compositions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Major Works and Achievements</strong><br>\nAmong Ravel's major works are the ballet \"Daphnis et Chloé,\" the orchestral piece \"Boléro,\" and the piano suite \"Gaspard de la nuit.\" His music is known for its rich color, melody, harmony, and inventive orchestration, which won him acclaim throughout France and beyond.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
