          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Contribution to Ballet and Opera</strong><br>\nRavel made significant contributions to the ballet genre, with works like \"Boléro\" and \"La Valse.\" He also composed operas, including \"L'heure espagnole,\" which showcased his talent for setting dramatic scenes to music with exquisite timing and atmosphere.</p>\n\n<p><strong>World War I Impact</strong><br>\nThe outbreak of World War I had a profound impact on Ravel. He served as a driver for the motor transport corps, and the war's carnage deeply affected his health and post-war compositions. His experiences during the war are reflected in the more somber tone of his later works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Fame and Tours</strong><br>\nRavel's fame crossed borders, and he toured Europe and the United States to great acclaim. His trips to North America in the 1920s broadened his influence and exposure, introducing new elements into his music and promoting his standing as a global composer.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
